WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
An AI agent that can draft a customer reply — and cannot
send it.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A support request arrives. Ordinary, low risk, no money
involved.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
The agent reads one named message and looks up the order
through a typed, read-only tool.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
The reply is grounded in a record. No record, no claim —
the run fails closed instead.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.000
A draft appears in the original thread, addressed to the
person who wrote in. Nothing is sent.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Reading mutated nothing: same labels, still unread, zero
sends.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Now a request that would move money.

8
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The agent stops at awaiting_approval and writes no
business row. It never had the permission to.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:55.000
A human decides, in a channel with no model in it.

10
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The approval is recorded — and business state is
byte-identical. Approving is not executing.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Execution is a separate, explicit command under a
separate login.

12
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.000
One write. One outcome notification. Replaying the
command changes nothing further.

13
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:30.000
AI can reason. It cannot authorize itself, and it cannot
write.
